 "id": "opaque/thinking-signature-beside-text/5m",
 "description": "One request. Message 1 holds a thinking signature of 25,000 bytes. The provider bills a signature as few tokens, so the library prices it at 1 token for 250 bytes: 100 tokens. The client body holds 1,000 + 2,000 text tokens and the signature. The operator cuts m2 from 2,000 to 500 tokens. The forwarded body is billed 1,000 + 100 + 500 = 1,600 tokens. The text ratio leaves the signature out: (1,600 - 100) tokens over (4,000 + 2,000) forwarded text bytes = 0.25 tokens a byte. The cut removes 6,000 bytes: 6,000 x 0.25 = 1,500 tokens saved, at the cache write tier. If the signature were counted as text, the ratio would be 1,600 / 31,000 = 0.052 and the saving 309 tokens.",
